file: "packages/editor/src/pending/comment_builder.ts"
doc: "Constructing a Comment, including the id everything else matches on."

methods: [
  { name: "newComment"
    doc:
      "Build a Comment with its id, author and timestamp filled in.\n"
      "\n"
      "ASYNC, and that is forced rather than chosen: Comment.id is specified\n"
      "as a sha256 prefix, the only digest available in the browser is\n"
      "crypto.subtle.digest, and it returns a Promise. Mirror\n"
      "state/stylesheet_hash.ts, which computes StyleEdit-adjacent hashes the\n"
      "same way -- canonical JSON, SHA-256, first 8 bytes as 16 hex\n"
      "characters. EditorState.addComment stays synchronous by taking the\n"
      "finished Comment rather than building one.\n"
      "\n"
      "WHY THE ID MATTERS. mergeThreads dedupes by it. A comment posted to a\n"
      "PR carries this id inside its metadata envelope and is parsed back out\n"
      "with the same id, so fetching after posting recognises the comment as\n"
      "one already held rather than appending a second copy. An id that did\n"
      "not round-trip would make every fetch duplicate every reply.\n"
      "\n"
      "The digest covers `body`, `author` and `timestampMs`. timestampMs is\n"
      "read from Date.now() INSIDE this function, so it is NOT a pure\n"
      "function of its two arguments: calling it twice with the same body and\n"
      "author in different milliseconds yields two different ids. The\n"
      "determinism that matters is over the digest's three values -- the same\n"
      "body, author and timestamp always hash to the same id, which is what\n"
      "makes a posted comment recognisable when it is fetched back.\n"
      "\n"
      "`author` is passed in rather than discovered. The editor has no\n"
      "signed-in user: edit_builder.ts already stamps its StyleEdits\n"
      "'user:local', and callers here pass the same. On a PR the forge also\n"
      "records its own author from the OAuth token, which is the identity a\n"
      "human reader sees; this field is what archeglyph's own parser reads\n"
      "back.\n"
      "\n"
      "replyTo is left unset. v1 threads are flat -- see ThreadView."
    inputs: [
      { name: "body",   type: { primitive: CHARACTER } },
      { name: "author", type: { primitive: CHARACTER } }
    ]
    is_async: true
    output: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.style.v1.Comment" } }
  }
]
